invariant: INV-70
file: src/p256_arm64_asm.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh p256-arm64
reason: p256_arm64_mul_mont's second round of the reduction drops the carry
  the first round left in the C flag, so a product whose first round
  carries comes out short by that bit times 2^64 at word 5, a value no
  longer congruent to the product. The square keeps the carry, so only
  products go wrong, in about one product in four. bin/p256_arm64_equiv_test
  compares each product with the model word for word, and the qemu lane
  runs it for arm64 under gcc.

--- old
        // Round 1, u = t1, at words 2 to 5. ADC adds the carry of round 0 to
        // the high word of u * p3. MUL, UMULH and LSR write no flag.
        "mul %[l0], %[t1], %[p3]\n"
        "umulh %[l1], %[t1], %[p3]\n"
        "lsr %[l2], %[t1], #0x20\n"
        "adc %[l1], %[l1], xzr\n"
--- new
        // Round 1, u = t1, at words 2 to 5. ADC adds the carry of round 0 to
        // the high word of u * p3. MUL, UMULH and LSR write no flag.
        "mul %[l0], %[t1], %[p3]\n"
        "umulh %[l1], %[t1], %[p3]\n"
        "lsr %[l2], %[t1], #0x20\n"
